{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Acceptance-criteria evaluation against `origin/main` at `5f618b3ccff`, run criterion by criterion. **Verdict: do not close. 2 of 8 checkable criteria are unmet, and a residue defect was found that no criterion covers.**\n\nPASS — AC1 (retired-id grep prints nothing), AC2 (`regenerate-index` then `git diff --exit-code` on `index.json`: no drift), AC5 (`rebar workflow validate src/rebar/llm/workflow/examples/review_skeleton.yaml` exits 0), AC6 (`tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py`: 5 passed), AC7 (the workflows-untouched grep quoted in Context: zero hits), AC8 (`python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` exits 0).\n\nNOT RUN — AC9 `make verify`. Every slice earned `Verified +1` individually, but that is not the same as a verify on this tip, so AC9 is recorded unverified rather than assumed.\n\nFAIL — AC3 and AC4, both for the same cause. AC3 requires `index.json` to contain exactly one `\"default\": true`, on `code-quality`; it contains **zero** — the 5 entries (`code-quality`, `completion-verifier`, `security`, `spec-alignment`, `tests`) carry no `default` key at all. AC4 requires `select_reviewers([])` to return `['code-quality']`; it returns `[]`.\n\nThe cause is a deliberate divergence from this plan, not an omission. This ticket's step 4 promotes `code_quality.md` to `default: true` because its Context reasoned that `prompts.py` raises unless exactly one default exists, so a replacement default was required. The slices instead **deleted the default-reviewer concept outright**, on the reasoning that only the retired single-pass engine consulted it. Confirmed in the tree: no reviewer prompt has a `default:` front-matter key, `prompts.py` has no default-reviewer logic, `select_reviewers` at `:607` is purely `applies_to`-glob driven, and `test_index_has_exactly_one_default` no longer exists. `docs/release-notes.md` records both halves — the \"exactly one `default: true` reviewer\" index invariant is removed, and `select_reviewers([])` now returns `[]` (was `['ticket-quality']`).\n\nSo AC3 and AC4 were superseded by a shipped, documented design decision. They are nonetheless unmet as written. Rewriting them now to match what shipped would manufacture the pass rather than earn it, so they are left standing and this ticket stays open pending an explicit disposition.\n\nResidue defect found while checking, filed as `ethologic-antisolar-queenbee` (`34ec-cd4e-5673-423a`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket: `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md` still documents the removed mechanism at `:42` (a `default` front-matter key table row, \"exactly one default; see §4\") and `:201` (\"**exactly one `default`** across reviewers\", stated as a validation violation). AC1's grep could not have caught it — its pattern covers `_review_ticket_impl`, `review_workflows`, `ticket-quality`, `ticket_quality`, `rebar-ticket-quality` and `aggregate_findings`, and never searches for `default`.\n\nAlso corrected here: this ticket is **not** blocked. Its sole `depends_on` target `dc42-a2ce-bee2-4da6` is closed, so `ticket_deps` reports `ready_to_work: true`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793383322645814600,"uuid":"969f8b6b-8585-440a-9ff9-17edfc8da133"}